Reading this:
- %Max compares to the vendor 'max' line; for writes %Sustained compares
  to the sustained line (the honest steady-state target).
- A read flagged CACHE? is NOT a valid cold number — its working set still
  fits server cache. Raise DEFEAT_TIB until the flag clears, then re-read.
- CLIENT-limited means add client nodes; STORAGE-limited means the product
  itself tops out below spec on this access path. Both are real findings.
- This is an aggregate-of-N-clients measurement. If the vendor quoted the
  spec with a specific client fleet, match that fleet for an apples-to-apples
  claim; otherwise report it explicitly as 'sustained by N client nodes'.

